From b82a682af71fa5288f947971da19564598703163 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:26:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] The fight under a blur, in your own eyes; an exhale with
 every blow; no hitches; a chapter turn lets the printed matter leave first

- Back to the first person: the camera stays in your eyes, the street breaks into pixels and blurs
  (lighter than before, so the blows show through), and the fight's animation (his side of it) plays
  under it: your flurry, the uppercut, him on his back. Every blow jolts the view and is heard
  with an exhale. The third-person camera and your drawn body are gone.
- Hitches: no light comes or goes any more (car headlights, the stranger's key light, the laundry
  light, the Mercedes' lamps are dimmed instead), so the street is never compiled again mid-scene;
  the street's materials are compiled as the chapter opens; pixel density only goes down;
  multisampling fixed at start.
- Chapter turn: his face, his thoughts, the tip and the captions leave through their own pixels
  (and fade) before the frame is copied and the scene turns.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017Yfam9H7FbQFsBx6yJZ8yW
